## What a `type: system-actor` instance is

**A system actor memorial describes an automated process that takes actions in the corpus.**  Distinct from AI actors (model-driven) and human actors (intentional collaboration) — system actors are deterministic / rule-driven processes:

- PreToolUse hooks — discipline-enforcement processes
- Inject hooks — advisory context-surfacing processes
- Post-commit hooks (e.g., index refresh, audit triggers)
- Audit-invariant runners
- Scheduled tasks / cron-driven processes
- Companion broker processes
- CI runners

System actor memorials make the **harness layer** itself a first-class graph citizen — discipline enforcement, capture, and audit are not just code but also memorialized entities that artifacts can be `performed-by:`.

System Actor is a subtype of [`actor`](actor.md) → [`meta`](meta.md).

