## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

System Actor memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` (and `actor`) plus system-specific slots:

- **`process-class`** (required) — `hook` / `scheduled-task` / `ci-runner` / `runner-broker` / `audit-invariant` / ...
- **`triggers`** — natural-language list of trigger conditions
- **`belongs-to`** — organization that owns this process (often "this corpus")
- **`runs-in-context`** — where this process operates
- **`implementation-path`** — rel-path to the source file (hook script / scheduler config / etc.)

{{slot-table}}

## Process-class vocabulary

- **`hook`** — fires synchronously on a lifecycle event (PreToolUse / PostCompact / SessionStart / etc.)
- **`scheduled-task`** — fires at scheduled intervals via cron-like scheduler
- **`ci-runner`** — runs in continuous-integration pipeline (test / lint / build / deploy)
- **`runner-broker`** — orchestrates other runners (multi-agent coordination)
- **`audit-invariant`** — fires when corpus audit runs; reports violations
- **`indexer`** — maintains a derived index (xref / search / aggregate)

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## What this process does

<Description of the automated action this process performs.>

## When it fires

<Trigger conditions: lifecycle event, schedule, manual invocation,
upstream signal.>

## Implementation

<Where the source lives, what language / runtime it uses, key
dependencies.>

## What it produces

<Side effects: memorials written, indices updated, files modified,
notifications emitted.>

## Operating contexts

<Where this process is permitted to run; firewall constraints.>

## See also

<Adjacent system actors, triggering events, governing rules.>
```

## Composition with adjacent classes

- **`event`** — system actors are typical triggers for substrate events (especially `post-commit`, `corpus-audit`, `pre-tool-use`)
- **`rule`** — rules may scope to specific system-actor process-classes
- **`organization`** — system actors typically `belongs-to` the corpus itself (or a tooling project)
- **`context`** — system actors run in specific contexts (CI / local / sandboxed)
- **`bug`** — bugs in system actor processes are tracked like any bug

